  body: "# Supersession in the DMG\n\n## Authored interpretation\n\nThe DMG describes supersession as replacing
    a decision from a later date, subject to grounds, and separates deciding whether an award changes from deciding
    the effective date and any overpayment.\n\n## Scope and exceptions\n\nThe chapter covers decisions of DMs and
    tribunals within specified conditions. The introductory description does not supply all benefit-specific effective-date
    rules; decisions that can be revised are treated separately.\n\n## Inspected source passages\n\n- [DMG 04000,
    PDF page 3](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6a105e7a1eb143220d8d27f1/dmg-ch-04.pdf#page=3) —
    DMG Vol 1 Ch 4: Supersession, suspension and termination .\n- [DMG 04009, PDF page 7](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6a105e7a1eb143220d8d27f1/dmg-ch-04.pdf#page=7)
    — DMG Vol 1 Ch 4: Supersession, suspension and termination .\n- [DMG 04050, PDF page 15](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6a105e7a1eb143220d8d27f1/dmg-ch-04.pdf#page=15)
    — DMG Vol 1 Ch 4: Supersession, suspension and termination .\n\n## Evidence and review status\n\nModel-assisted
    interpretation of the 15 September 2026 source snapshot; unreviewed and requiring specialist review. The source
    is DWP guidance, not a consolidated statement of legislation. This is an independent experimental publication,
    not an official DWP document, an entitlement decision or an executable benefits rule.\n\nPDF page numbers are
    one-based file positions. Machine extraction can alter reading order, footnotes and characters. Quoted relationships
    preserve extracted text; no visual or specialist acceptance is claimed. Source dates, legal effects and current
    applicability remain separate review tasks.\n\n- `dmg-vol1-ch4` PDF SHA-256: `9c96b49a78aa4dc40df8594cf65cbd435a681d0be3737729cd87882542d0e2ea`;
    extracted pages SHA-256: `bef5fc9f04b2a78c5bb5dc99468f94a1841f1ef4afa117d47aa9c1e5040f3752`.\n"
  semantic_relations:
  - target: term/dmg-supersession-effective-date
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: Determining when a supersession takes effect is an explicit task within the described process.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol1-ch4/0015
      quote: "04050 Once it has been decided that there are grounds for supersession, the DM should\n\n\n1. identify
        the decision to be superseded\n\n\n2. investigate and determine the relevant facts\n\n\n3. decide whether
        the facts mean that the terms of the award should change\n\n\n4. make a decision accordingly. That may be
        either a decision which is different from the decision\nsuperseded or a decision not to supersede\n\n\n\
        5. determine the date from which the supersession decision should take effect\n\n\n6. decide what, if any,
        overpayment has occurred."
      locator: DMG 04050
  - target: term/dmg-overpayment-recoverability
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The supersession process includes considering whether an overpayment occurred; occurrence alone
      does not establish recoverability.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol1-ch4/0015
      quote: "04050 Once it has been decided that there are grounds for supersession, the DM should\n\n\n1. identify
        the decision to be superseded\n\n\n2. investigate and determine the relevant facts\n\n\n3. decide whether
        the facts mean that the terms of the award should change\n\n\n4. make a decision accordingly. That may be
        either a decision which is different from the decision\nsuperseded or a decision not to supersede\n\n\n\
        5. determine the date from which the supersession decision should take effect\n\n\n6. decide what, if any,
        overpayment has occurred."
